<b>Origin</b>
Cheech is based on Gnome Chinese Checkers by Loban Rahman. The game
engine derives from his code:

    Gnome Chinese Checkers (gchch)
    Copyright (C) 1999-2003 Loban Rahman
    GNU General Public License, version 2 or later
    <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/gchch/">https://sourceforge.net/projects/gchch/</a>

<b>Linked libraries</b>
Cheech is built with and links against many free software libraries.
The macOS bundle includes copies of the libraries listed below; on
other systems they are provided by your operating system. All are
copyright their respective authors.

<b>GNU LGPL 2.1 or later</b>
• gtkmm, glibmm, giomm, pangomm, cairomm, libsigc++
• GTK, GLib, Pango, GDK-Pixbuf
• FriBidi, libthai, libdatrie
• gettext (libintl)

<b>Dual-licensed</b>
• Cairo — LGPL 2.1 or MPL 1.1
• FreeType — FreeType License (BSD-style) or GPL 2
• zstd — BSD 3-clause or GPL 2

<b>Permissive licences</b>
• HarfBuzz — Old MIT license
• Graphene, libepoxy — MIT
• pixman, fontconfig, libtiff — MIT-style
• libwebp, pcre2 — BSD 3-clause
• brotli — MIT
• liblzma (xz) — 0BSD / public domain
• X11 and xcb — MIT/X11
• libpng — PNG Reference Library License
• libjpeg — BSD 3-clause and IJG-style

<b>GNU GPL 2 or later</b>
• liblzo2 — a dependency of GTK's copy of cairo; its source is
  available at
  <a href="https://www.oberhumer.com/opensource/lzo/">https://www.oberhumer.com/opensource/lzo/</a>

